---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url, REPO } from '../lib/url';
const site = new URL(url(), Astro.site).href;
const title = 'Whichart for AI agents: chart rules, code and review as tools | Whichart';
const description = 'Give your coding agent Whichart: an MCP server and Agent Skill that recommend the right chart for your data, return tested code with edge-case rules, and review a chart before it ships.';
const tools = [
  ['recommend_chart', 'Data or a schema, plus an optional goal and space → ranked charts with reasons, and an avoid list.'],
  ['get_chart', 'Chart id and library → guidance, edge-case rules and ready code.'],
  ['list_charts', 'Every written chart, filtered by goal or industry, with the builder questions each one answers.'],
  ['review_chart', '“Is this chart right for this data?” → a verdict, problems and better options. Call it before showing any chart.'],
];
const RAW = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Whichart/whichart.github.io/main';
const npx = '"command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "@whichart/mcp"]';
const setups: [string, string, string][] = [
  ['Claude Code', 'terminal', 'claude mcp add whichart -- npx -y @whichart/mcp'],
  ['Cursor', '.cursor/mcp.json', `{ "mcpServers": { "whichart": { ${npx} } } }`],
  ['VS Code', '.vscode/mcp.json', `{ "servers": { "whichart": { "type": "stdio", ${npx} } } }`],
  ['Windsurf', '~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json', `{ "mcpServers": { "whichart": { ${npx} } } }`],
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="wrap ag">
    <h1>For AI agents</h1>
    <p class="lede">Agents write most chart code now, and they often pick the wrong chart or miss the edge cases. Whichart gives them the same rules people see on this site, as files and tools.</p>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>MCP server</h2>
      <p class="muted">Four tools, bundled with every chart, guide and code sample. It runs on your machine, needs no key, and your data never leaves it.</p>
      <table>
        <tbody>{tools.map(([name, what]) => <tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{what}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>Set up</h3>
      <p class="note">The npm package <code>@whichart/mcp</code> is being published. Until it is, use the <a href="#source">from-source setup</a> below; the commands here will work as soon as it’s live.</p>
      {setups.map(([name, where, code]) => (
        <div class="setup">
          <h4>{name} <span class="muted">{where}</span></h4>
          <pre><code>{code}</code></pre>
        </div>
      ))}
      <h4 id="source">From source (works today)</h4>
      <pre><code>{`git clone ${REPO} && cd whichart.github.io
pnpm install && pnpm --filter @whichart/mcp build
claude mcp add whichart -- node "$PWD/packages/mcp/dist/index.js"`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Agent Skill</h2>
      <p class="muted">The tools work best when your agent knows when to call them. The <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/skill`}>Whichart skill</a> tells it to recommend before it charts, build from the tested code and edge-case rules, and call <code>review_chart</code> before showing a chart it chose itself.</p>
      <pre><code>{`mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills/whichart
curl -fsSL ${RAW}/skill/whichart/SKILL.md -o ~/.claude/skills/whichart/SKILL.md`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Files for any agent</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li><a href={url('llms.txt')}><code>/llms.txt</code></a>: an index of every chart and pattern.</li>
        <li><a href={url('llms-full.txt')}><code>/llms-full.txt</code></a>: every chart in full, rules, edge cases and code, in one file.</li>
        <li><a href={url('charts/line.md')}><code>/charts/&lt;id&gt;.md</code></a>: one chart as Markdown, the same text <code>get_chart</code> returns.</li>
        <li><a href={url('catalog.json')}><code>/catalog.json</code></a>: every chart’s data-shape rules, fit rules and context fit, as JSON.</li>
        <li>The recommendation engine on the command line: <code>pnpm whichart data.csv --goal trend</code> (<a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/packages/engine`}>docs</a>).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>No tools? Tell your agent</h2>
      <p class="muted">Add this to its instructions (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .cursorrules):</p>
      <pre><code>Before adding a chart, check {site}llms.txt for the right chart type,
then read its page at {site}charts/&lt;id&gt;.md: follow its edge cases
(empty data, zeros, no previous period, gaps in time) and start from
its code. Never use a dual y-axis.</code></pre>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .ag h1 { font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px); margin: 24px 0 8px; }
  .lede { font-size: 18px; max-width: 64ch; color: var(--wc-ink-secondary); }
  .list li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14px; }
  td { padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--wc-grid); vertical-align: top; }
  .note { background: var(--wc-surface); border: 1px solid var(--wc-border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 14px; }
  h4 { margin: 18px 0 6px; font-size: 15px; }
  h4 .muted { font-weight: 400; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 6px; }
  pre { background: var(--wc-surface); border: 1px solid var(--wc-border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; overflow-x: auto; }
</style>
